      "challenges": [
        "Persistent weak contact follow-up around confirmed cases in Bas-Uele and Haut-Uele, attributed to insufficient dedicated teams.",
        "Insufficient PoE/PoC operationalisation: 84.8% report completeness (106/125), with Sud-Kivu 55.5%, Bas-Uele 60% and Haut-Uele 64%; only 1 of 11 strategic Ituri points operated uninterrupted and Avakubi remains non-functional for security reasons.",
        "Weak IPC implementation: Ituri household decontamination limited to 67.0% with no IPC kits supplied, decontamination teams short at Fataki, Mangala and Nizi; Tshopo reports insufficient PPE, untrained providers and a broken incinerator at HGR Makiso-Kisangani.",
        "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu exceeded capacity at 107.3%, with some suspects isolated in facilities that are not treatment centres; Bas-Uele has no compliant CTE and no case-management support partner.",
        "Community resistance persists in Ituri: an isolation refusal at Nia-Nia and a safe-burial refusal in Lolwa health zone.",
        "Insufficient MHPSS coverage: Haut-Uele under-covered, only 4 Nord-Kivu zones covered with no CTE creches, and Ituri covering 5 of 11 reporting zones (45%) with none at Bambu, Nia-Nia, Mambasa or Lolwa.",
        "Incomplete PoC security: a body intercepted at Magambe PoC (Isiro) was released without being swabbed, and Nord-Kivu burial-area insecurity persists with the Bundji cemetery road impassable.",
        "PSEA coverage remains insufficient: 25% of Ituri health zones (9/36) know the reporting mechanism and only WHO and IMC report PSEA activities."
      ],
